      <title>Government Entitles to Interest when Tax Paid after Statutory Due Date but Return Filed within Time limit: Bombay HC [Read Order]</title>
      <link>https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/government-entitles-to-interest-when-tax-paid-after-statutory-due-date-but-return-filed-within-time-limit-bombay-hc-1440935</link>
      <description>The bench observed that under Section 25(4), interest becomes payable from the date the tax becomes due, whenever tax shown as payable in returns or revised returns is not paid or is paid belatedly.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/government-entitles-to-interest-when-tax-paid-after-statutory-due-date-but-return-filed-within-time-limit-bombay-hc-1440935</guid>
